  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The layering rule",
      "items": [
        "Nothing links upward: each library compiles against the ones below it and knows nothing of the ones above.",
        "ToyFrontend has no idea MLIR exists: ldd on the unit-test binary lists no MLIR library."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What the dialect is made of",
      "items": [
        "Ops.td declares one dialect, one type and twelve operations. mlir-tblgen turns it into accessors, builders, verifiers, parser and printer.",
        "Canonicalization patterns live with the dialect; with the passes, the two archives became mutually dependent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why the gate is the point",
      "items": [
        "The language is unchanged, so our output can be required to match toyc-ch7 byte for byte at every stage.",
        "18,480 comparisons, 0 unexpected, nothing skipped. A mutant that renames toy.mul fails the sweep."
      ]
    }
  ]
